      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "West Eau Claire, founded in 1856 across the river, became the county courthouse site and was incorporated in 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eau_Claire%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The University of Wisconsin–Eau Claire opened in 1916, shifting the city from lumber to manufacturing, education, and healthcare.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
